Figure 3: Comparison between rest-frame \(850\,\mu{m}\) dust continuum luminosity and CO(1–0) luminosity. Left : \(L^{\prime}_{CO(1-0)}\) as a function of \(L_{
u}(850\,\mu{m})\) for the ACE galaxies, compared to the empirical calibration of Scoville et al. (2016) , the local universe (plusses) and \(z\sim 2\) measurements (crosses) of Scoville et al. (2016) and to individual measurements from Kaasinen et al. (2019) (triangles) and ASPECS ( Boogaard et al., 2020 ) (squares). The dashed line shows the constant \(\alpha_{850}=6.7	imes 10^{19}\,{erg\,s^{-1}\,Hz^{-1}\,M_{\odot}^{-1}}\) calibration from Scoville et al. (2016) , while the solid line shows their luminosity-dependent form, \(\alpha_{850}=6.2	imes 10^{19}L_{
u,31}(850\,\mu{m})^{0.07}\) . Right : ratio \(L_{
u}(850\,\mu{m})/L^{\prime}_{CO(1-0)}\) as a function of \(L_{
u}(850\,\mu{m})\) , showing the same calibrations. ACE and ASPECS galaxies are colour-coded by metallicity. The ACE sources lie broadly within the scatter of the literature relation, and the ratio plot shows no clear systematic trend with \(L_{
u}(850\,\mu{m})\) or metallicity over the range probed here.

